  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BETWEEN JERUSALEM AND BELFAST: LEARNING LESSONS TO IMPACT POLICY CHANGE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TJ&apos;s project seeks to protect and preserve the political, religious, territorial, and cultural character of Palestinian East Jerusalem. To this end, this project will revisit Belfast. The stark parallels between Jerusalem and Belfast have been studied extensively, and the perils of drawing simplistic comparisons are duly noted. However, major shifts in Jerusalem dynamics warrant further analysis towards developing and impacting policy. Such developments require this: a) ascendancy of the faith dimension; b) increase in violent, intercommunal skirmishing; c) nature of policing in East Jerusalem and, d) disempowerment of vulnerability communities</narrative>
  </description>
